# seed: 1
# requires: hero_ready spell_learn spell_cast music_play
# requires-match: spell_cast caster=hero
# requires-match: spell_cast caster=monster
#
# STATUS: the route is authored and verified end to end up to the Spell Training master
# (SCENE 291, reached, spoken to and left); the three spell assertions are NOT yet met.
# Everything below is measured on the pinned binary, not inferred.
#
# The Gateway of Dreams is answered, not walked past. quest.txt:1774 is `ASK 30` - the golden
# rule - and an ASK suspends the scene until the player answers, so the script answers it the
# way a player does, with Y (scene.c's ST_ASK sets the reply to "YES"). The Soul Brother hands
# over L1 / H5000 / M5000, opens the `OFFER2 0,10` shop and sizes the trophy bag to 4x3, and
# music.ini [evergreen] gives the map_enter music_play.
#
# PP IS THE WHOLE PROBLEM, and the floor is exact. FUN_0047FCED (world.c complete_spells)
# seeds pp at 5000 and grows it 1.5x per required-affinity level, then FUN_0047FCF7 divides by
# 20: the cheapest spell in retail Evergreen is spell 1 "Dirt" at affinity 0, so 5000/20 =
# 250 PP, and spells.txt gives no spell an explicit lower price (every row checked: the ppCost
# column is 0 = auto everywhere except the unlearnable -1s). PP is earned at battle.c:1270,
# `hero_add_pp(hero, WIS*200/255+5)` once per committed hero action. Six `key DOWN` in the
# Pick-a-Soul window pick class 7, whose levels.txt START_ABILITY gives WIS 10, so 12 PP an
# action and 21 actions for one spell; the default class 1 Sword-User has `hero.abil.wis=0` in
# the dump, so 5 PP an action and 50 actions. No scene in the world does `GIVE P<n>` (grep
# over every extracted/worlds/Evergreen script finds none), and the only scripted PP is
# missions.ini [1] "Jelly Bellies" (RewardPP=1000), which needs 5x trophy 1 "Green Jelly
# Pigment" at a 5 % drop.
#
# The deterministic PP farm the retail data offers is the training masters, because their loss
# branches heal and re-fight with no walking:
#     map 2 link 12 -> SCENE 290 "Hand Training"  (QuestScenes200.txt:1173)
#         @1 MOVE / FIGHT 1 / IF ALIVE,@2 / 22 `'` lines / @3 MOVE / FIGHT 1, 4 / IF ALIVE,@4
#         / on a loss six `'` lines / GIVE L1 H5000 M5000 / GOTO @3
#     map 2 link 11 -> SCENE 291 "Spell Training" (QuestScenes200.txt:1317)
#         IF T2,@1 ... @1 FIGHT 1 / IF ALIVE,@2 / eight `'` lines / GIVE L1 H5000 M5000 /
#         GOTO @1 ... and on a win `GIVE S207`, a free known spell to cast with.
# Both links are reached below. Measured on the binary, a caster (class 7) walking SCENE 290's
# `FIGHT 1, 4` loss loop banks 24 PP an iteration - two committed hero actions - so 250 PP is
# about eleven iterations of [press A, take the six dialogue lines, get healed, fight again].
# The loop measured only 108 PP over nine iterations before the hero stopped committing
# actions, so the remaining work is to find the iteration count that actually reaches 250 and
# then to survive a fight long enough to cast. SCENE 291 is gated on T2, the token at the end
# of the whole Hand Training chain, so its `GIVE S207` route is the fallback for
# `spell_cast caster=hero` once the chain is finished.
expect boot_menu 900
key RETURN
wait 30
key RETURN
wait 30
key RETURN
wait 30
key n
wait 5
text SpellStudent
key RETURN
expect hero_ready 300
expect map_enter 600
keydown DOWN
expect scene_enter 600
keyup DOWN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
key y
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
